cpumon (1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New: top CPU-consuming processes, per-core frequency, CPU temperature
    and CPU pressure (PSI) readings.
  * New: usage-history sparklines in the interactive displays.
  * New: JSON Lines and CSV output (--format) for --once and log files.
  * New: high-usage alerts (--alert, --alert-duration) via syslog, the log
    file and an on-screen banner.
  * New: gzip compression of old logs (--compress-after-days) and --replay
    with --since/--until to print logged history.
  * New: systemd journal output (--log-target journal|both).
  * New: config files (/etc/cpumon/cpumon.conf, ~/.config/cpumon/cpumon.conf,
    --config); the daemon re-reads its config on SIGHUP and the unit gains
    ExecReload.
  * Fix: make install points the systemd unit at the installed binary.
  * Add unit and smoke tests (run during the package build) and CI.

 -- Shabbir Yusufali <shabyusufali@gmail.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 19:54:41 +0000

